{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>All your border.</b> And not the border of Ham. And here the plagues were making known the boundaries of the land. And so they said in the Midrash: the sons of Ham and the sons of Mizraim were divided over the boundaries — the Cushites saying, 'Up to here is our border,' and the Egyptians saying, 'Up to here is our border.' Once the frogs came, they made peace between them: the border in which there were no frogs, they knew that it was not of Egypt, as it is said, 'All your border' — and not of others."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:53.890717389Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}